  "ref": "EZK.45.17",
  "review_notes": [
    "The obligation clause is divided as: עַל → *part* (the relation the ASV spends a word on), הַנָּשִׂיא → *the prince’s*, יִהְיֶה → *it shall be*, and the supplied lexical verb *to give* `added` under rule 20. A competing reading folds *to give* into the עַל unit; I kept it `added` because no source verb licenses it."
  ]
